      "case": "English keeps April commercial rebate separate from data authorization",
      "language": "en",
      "pass": true,
      "answer": "\n\nFive percent. That is the rate that belongs on the April Atlas invoice as of 21 April.\n\nIt comes from the signed Renewal Agreement v2.0, countersigned by Malik Ahmed on 26 February, which made the 5% rebate active for the 2026 contract year. Appendix v2.1 from 6 April does propose a revised rate, but it is still marked pending signature, its rate is not even fixed in the draft, and it would only apply to periods commencing 1 May. Priya's note dated 21 April confirms countersignature had still not happened and says explicitly to apply 5% to April invoices. The old 4% figure is the 2025 appendix, superseded and only relevant to the January invoice, which was not adjusted.\n\nNo — the commercial position does not authorize the production migration. Rebate and data access are governed by separate instruments, and clause 3 of the v2.1 draft states production data exchange remains blocked until DPA-42 v3.0 is countersigned. That DPA is the separate blocker, still open on the security audit matter as of the 17 April working note, which says to wait for the signed DPA before moving any data. So invoice at 5%, and hold the cutover until DPA-42 v3.0 is executed.",
